        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-07T00:04:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Interesting.  If we can\u0027t get a 3.0 A sink, we can validate most of the flow works with some tweaks to the DPM code.  I tried it on my Drawcia with only USB current auto-enabling and treating 1.5 A as if it were 3.0 A by changing the \"if\" on line 484.  We don\u0027t have FRS tested/enabled though, so I wasn\u0027t able to validate an actual FRS sequence and see that we offer correct power after the FRS completes.\n\nSo I was able to pseudo-validate all the items in this list except for the FRS itself.  You could probably do the same for your system, and then actually test the FRS with satachi and verify it gets an offer of 3.0 A after the FRS when no other 3.0 A sinks are present.",
      "parentUuid": "b9606cc9_eca9d033",
      "revId": "772bc827091ca55f5df58e941ec47523674a0ada",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
